[2026-03-29 00:52:12] Refactored SCB interrupts to use a report-first flow instead of direct UART exception printing.
- Request: Verify whether SCB still had the same legacy issue as SYSEXC and implement the same report-stage plus custom-stage pattern for all SCB interrupts.
- Investigation: Confirmed that BusFault, MemoryFault, UsageFault, and HardFault still used direct UART configuration and UART__uxCustomPrintf-based __vSendValues() helpers, with GNU/TI vector stubs calling those helpers before the custom handlers. Also checked NMI and found it did not use UART, but it still lacked the same report/custom stage split.
- Implementation: Added the shared SCB report API under xApplication_MCU/Core/SCB/xHeader/SCB_Report.h and xSource/SCB_Report.c, exported it through xApplication_MCU/Core/SCB/SCB.h, and refactored BusFault, MemoryFault, UsageFault, HardFault, and NMI to create SCB_REPORT_t payloads in dedicated report-stage handlers while keeping source-clear and callback dispatch in custom-stage handlers.
- Vector integration: Updated GNU and TI assembly stubs for BusFault, MemoryFault, UsageFault, and HardFault so they now call <Fault>__vIRQVectorHandlerReport(...) first and <Fault>__vIRQVectorHandlerCustom(...) second, mirroring the SYSEXC assembly flow.
- HardFault detail: Added SCB_enFAULT_HARD to SCB_nFAULT and kept the forced-fault routing semantics by delegating HardFault forced cases into the BusFault, MemoryFault, or UsageFault report/custom handlers instead of flattening them into a generic hard-fault print path.
- Validation: VS Code diagnostics report no errors in TM4C129E_DriverLib/xApplication_MCU/Core/SCB after the refactor. Remaining __vSendValues hits are limited to generated Release__TI artifacts and not active source files.